ase. It then formed a base for about 4 weeks, peaking at $23.98 and pulling back 9% at its deepest. Daily price ranges tightened on the right side of the base.","outcome":"On Jan 30, 2024 it closed at $24.03, its first close above the base high of $23.98. Volume that day was 7.3M shares, 1.46x the prior 10-day average of 5.0M. It held, never closing below the level three days running, reached a best close of $30.64, and the chart ends at $27.01.","lesson":"This is an example of a textbook breakout: a base, then a close above it on heavy volume, and it held. This is the pattern the rules are built around."}}